  "result": "Perfect! All 197 tests pass. I've successfully implemented credit notes:\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH`: \"Credit note amount exceeds the invoice total.\"\n\n**Created `src/credits.js`** with two functions:\n\n**`nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, date)`** \u2014 generates credit note numbers:\n- Format: `CN-<year>-<counter>` (e.g., CN-2025-0001)\n- Counter starts at 0001, zero-padded to 4 digits\n- Separate counter for each year\n- Ignores invoice numbers (only counts CN numbers)\n- Tracks both invoice and credit note numbers together\n\n**`createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)`** \u2014 creates a credit note:\n- Returns `ok(creditNote)` with structure:\n  - `number`: CN-<year>-<counter>\n  - `invoiceNumber`: original invoice's number\n  - `customerId`: from the invoice\n  - `amount`: refund amount in cents\n  - `reason`: reason for credit\n  - `date`: credit note issue date\n- Returns errors:\n  - `NOT_ISSUED` if invoice status is 'draft'\n  - `AMOUNT_INVALID` if amount isn't a positive integer\n  - `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` if amount exceeds invoice total\n- Works on invoices with status: 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n\n**Added 16 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- CN number generation (starting, incrementing, year-based)\n- Handling mixed invoice/credit note numbers\n- Unordered input handling\n- Credit note creation on different invoice statuses\n- Draft invoice rejection (NOT_ISSUED)\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, decimal)\n- Credit amount limits (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH and equality cases)\n- Multiple credits per invoice\n- Year changes in numbering\n- Customer ID preservation\n\nAll 197 tests pass (181 previous + 16 new). Credit notes are now fully functional for invoice refunds.",
